To do:
  - /etc/systemd/system/yubikey-anycast.service, installed by hand, hides the
    package's unit (which runs /opt/radiator-yubikey/yubikey-anycast.sh). To
    use the package's:
      sudo systemctl disable yubikey-anycast.service
      sudo rm /etc/systemd/system/yubikey-anycast.service
      sudo systemctl daemon-reload
      sudo systemctl enable yubikey-anycast.service
      sudo systemctl try-restart yubikey-anycast.service
  - /etc/systemd/system/yubikey-partition.service, installed by hand, hides
    the package's unit (which runs
    /opt/radiator-yubikey/yubikey-partition.sh). To use the package's:
      sudo rm /etc/systemd/system/yubikey-partition.service
      sudo systemctl daemon-reload
  - /usr/local/sbin/yubikey-db.sh /usr/local/sbin/yubikey-partition.sh:
    copies installed by hand, which the package's units don't use. Remove
    them when nothing else does.

Something is left to do.
[exit 1]

